{"unit": "vba:CairnReports.CommissionPeriod", "has_rules": true, "text": "CommissionPeriod() (CairnReports L498-500) returns the module-level period label for the currently open commission/RMA report: `CommissionPeriod = IIf(Len(mPeriod), mPeriod, "All dates")`. Rule: if the private module variable mPeriod (L31, "month shown on the commission statement") is non-empty, the function returns it verbatim; if it is empty, it returns the literal string "All dates".

Lifecycle evidence: mPeriod is set to Format(d1, "mmmm yyyy") (e.g. "March 2025") in PrintCommission (L486) and the RMA summary (L444) just before opening the report; it is reset to "" by ClearCommissionPeriod (L494-496), which is wired to every report's OnClose (L528: R.OnClose = "=ClearCommissionPeriod()"). Report headers/footers display it via =CommissionPeriod() (L208, L261, L279, L381, L409). So a report opened without a month (or after close) shows "All dates".

Testable rule (pure): commission_period(m_period) -> String: empty input => "All dates"; non-empty input (e.g. "March 2025") => the input unchanged.", "follow": []}

